// =================================================================================================
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This is a SimpleSal App developed and published by TSC LLC to demonstrate SimpleSal App features.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This App demonstrates the level of complexity SimpleSal supports: more than loop, less than RTOS.
// SimpleSal's Time and Event API helps solve complex problems a looping baremetal algorithm can't.
// Real device or system software problems are advanced implementations of the ideas within ssTEA.
// The solutions are simplified versions of RTOS or OS algorithms: Time- and Event-based software.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This minimum App demonstrates software in a legacy App interacting with ssTEA and ssUI real-time.
// The App's (forced) design: App's loop emits signals causing ssTEA to grant Events Agency.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Imagine a dangerously stupid machine which signals every 5 seconds "I am executing my software",
// by asserting a value on a shared communication link such as a wire on a board or a network port.
// If the dangerously stupid machine does not signal it is working, the App powers off the machine.
// Each time the App reads a signal from the machine, the signal is turned off, ready for the next.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The demonstration of ssTEA includes
//
//      a Time Event to check the state at some point in Time, a Time Event that does not recur.
//      a Data Event to display data generated by the Time Event, when signaled by the Time Event.
//      a Time Event that recurs each second, each recurrence decrements a counter if nonzero; if
//           counter transitions from nonzero to zero: ssUI is used to show the current statistics.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// =================================================================================================
