// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// allocation of per-Event data in ssTEA and ssUI is all based on SSE_ACTIVE_EVENTS_CT_REQUESTED.
// These defines simply assign the ownership of each ssUI EvApi data structure to an array Index.
// This model supports the address of data being computed at run time by a function, not build time.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// F14B56      specific configurations of EvApi allocations cause a hard fault in the App
//    requesting allocation of 3 EvApis and use the order 0,1,2: a quiet hard fault occurs.
//    changing order from 0,1,2 to 2,1,0: changed behavior from quiet brick to fault display.
//      address being accessed ends in 0xA, which is 10, which is not a multiple of 4.
//      LR link register is 67C1, the address of the caller of the code causing the fault
//    requesting allocation of 6 EvApis and using 2,1,0 or 2,1,0 order: hard fault does NOT occur.
//      this strongly suggests that a reference beyond the EvApi[0,1,2] is made by the statistics,
//      referring to memory after EvApi[2] ends hits EvApi[3,4,5]; instead of another variable.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#define     TIMEevent_EVENT_API             (2)
#define     DATAevent_EVENT_API             (1)
#define     STATSevent_EVENT_API            (0)

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The (forced) App tracks the full cycle using millisecond Timekeeping, the Duty cycle using ssTEA.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// An alternative allocation of ssTEA variables, as supported by ssTEA, is to use ssUI's free ones.
